Capabilities: Agent

Purpose:
  Defines agent technical capabilities. Capability is what agent
  CAN do technically; permission is whether it MAY do it under
  current policy.

Capabilities:
  READ:
    Description: Read files
    Risk: R0
  WRITE:
    Description: Create/update files
    Risk: R1
  DELETE:
    Description: Delete files
    Risk: R2
  MOVE:
    Description: Move/rename files
    Risk: R1
  EXECUTE:
    Description: Run commands
    Risk: R1
  TEST:
    Description: Run tests
    Risk: R1
  BUILD:
    Description: Build artifacts
    Risk: R1
  DOCKER:
    Description: Docker operations
    Risk: R2
  GIT:
    Description: Git operations
    Risk: R1
  DATABASE:
    Description: Database operations
    Risk: R2
  NETWORK:
    Description: Network operations
    Risk: R2
  DEPLOY:
    Description: Deployment operations
    Risk: R4

CapabilityRules:
  [CAP1]  Capability is technical ability, not permission.
  [CAP2]  Permission policy determines whether capability may be used.
  [CAP3]  Risk level is inherent to capability, not context.

State: +
  
